      "question": "Are food stamps the same as SNAP?",
      "answer": "The monthly grocery benefit a household spends with an EBT card is called SNAP. USDA's SNAP eligibility and eligible-food pages use the SNAP name throughout. EBT is the card that carries SNAP benefits, while WIC uses its own eWIC card."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I receive SNAP and WIC together?",
      "answer": "Yes, a family that meets both programs' rules can receive SNAP and WIC at the same time. USDA says SNAP participants may already be income eligible for WIC. The person enrolling in WIC still has to fit a WIC participant category, apply through a local WIC agency and complete a nutrition assessment with WIC staff."
